{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38556-can-animal-messanger-be-used-for-tracking-down-people","id":38556,"title":"Can Animal Messanger be used for tracking down people?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-28T20:19:25-08:00","id":38556,"title":"Can Animal Messanger be used for tracking down people?","content":"So lets say a Demon hears that the secretive Deva Corp Operative, Agent M, is in town, carrying a copy of the God Machine Manual.<br /> He doesn't have the contacts/streetwise to nail him down to any kind of location,<br /> but he does have the animal messenger embed.<br /> <br /> Can he say to his dog, &quot;Tell Agent M, I am coming for him.&quot; using the Animal Messanger Embed,<br /> then follow the dog til the dog finds Agent M?<br /> <br /> By RAW, this seems do-able.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Animal Messenger<br /> The demon can send an animal to a specified person with a message. The animal doesn\u2019t speak and<br /> cannot produce writing, but even by barking, chirping or yowling, the animal communicates what the<br /> demon needs it to say. Once the animal has delivered the message, it reverts to its usual behaviors<br /> (meaning it probably runs off). <br /> The animal has to be able to reach the target within a day; if it takes longer than that, the effect of the<br /> Embed wears off and animal reverts to normal behavior. The demon is therefore advised to choose fast,<br /> mobile, and socially acceptable animals. Collies are a popular choice. <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Manipulation + Animal Ken<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The animal runs off and delivers a message to the intended target, but the message is<br /> diametrically opposed to what the demon wanted. The animal might tell the target that someone that<br /> she cares about is dead (when the real message is that the person in question is alive and healthy), or<br /> that everything is fine when, in fact, the demon requires assistance. <br /> Failure: No effect; the animal continues behaving as normal. The demon can try again (apply a<br /> cumulative \u20131 penalty for each successive attempt on the same animal). <br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The animal runs, scampers, or flies off to deliver the message. It finds the target (waiting<br /> outside a building if necessary), and then \u201cspeaks\u201d by making whatever sounds it can. The target, if a<br /> normal human, is astonished to realize that he understands what the animal is trying to convey, but<br /> since the animal isn\u2019t literally speaking, the target doesn\u2019t feel fear or disbelief. The target is under no<br /> compulsion to act on the animal\u2019s message.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The animal remains with the target for a scene after delivering the message,<br /> nudging him to take whatever action the demon wishes and helping him stay on task. In game terms,<br /> the demon\u2019s player can portray the animal and provide suggestions to the target, if need be. </div> </div> </div>But I don't think this is right.<br /> The dog doesn't have any way of finding Agent M<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I would say that the animal is not given super natural ability to find the target.<br /> At best, it goes about finding it with human levels of intellect.<br /> <br /> So if it were given, one of Agent M's socks, it would track him down by scent.<br /> If shown a photo it would go around (for it's day) looking at people, in a systematic fasion to attempt to find and deliver the message.<br /> If it happened to know Agent M, personally, Eg if it was Agent M's dog, that hte demon some how stole, then it could find Agent M intimately.<br /> <br /> Just otherwise this power is more useful as a person finder than it is as a messenger","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T03:08:03-08:00","id":38648,"title":"","content":"Okay, so the key statement in this power is &quot;If it takes longer than [a day to reach the target], the effect of the Embed wears off and animal reverts to normal behaviour&quot;.<br /> I'd personally interpret that the time spent trying to find the target is counted within those 24 hours. You send Lassie to tell Agent M you're coming for him, and from then on, Lassie has to use her own skills to find Agent M. Thanks to the power, within those 24 hours, she has some supernatural idea of Agent M's characteristics that she however can't communicate (like his scent and appearance), but she still has to track him down, and that might involve spending the whole day to find a suitable scent to track.<br /> You could, in the meanwhile, follow Lassie, but no guarantee you'll find your target.<br /> I'd rule that following the Animal Messenger to find the target is a reasonable use of this power, but that you're likely to have penalties if the target has good reasons not to be found in time (like, well, being a Deva Corp agent), or if your animal is hard to follow/track down (good luck following Lassie if she's a pigeon or a bee), and that you'd get bonuses if you can give the animal useful information such as scent or appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T06:40:22-08:00","id":38706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/38556-can-animal-messanger-be-used-for-tracking-down-people?p=38648#post38648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally interpret that the time spent trying to find the target is counted within those 24 hours. You send Lassie to tell Agent M you're coming for him, and from then on, Lassie has to use her own skills to find Agent M.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is basically my ruling.<br /> <br /> I am instead giving the character the option of taking a cyptid hound as a 2 dot retainer.<br /> 1 dot for being a animal retainer, +1 extra dot for being a weak cryptid (Rank 1).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">The crypid has one Adaption: &quot;&#91;B&#93;Read the Logs&#91;/B&#93;&quot; A sys-admin, wanting to findout if the system has been hacked, can read the computers logs to find evidence of the intruder. Some god machine infrastructure can do the same thing, reading the logs for the universe. A certain pack of dogs, spent too much time near such infrastructure and picked that up, along with other cyptid traits. Cyptids breed true and Reading the Logs has proved useful for hunting prey and avoiding predictors. By Reading the Logs, the cryptid can find the information signiture of a person. Reading the Logs functions alot like a 6th sense, the hound notices unlike the convention senses, it is much harder to fool. (Works in the dark, in noisy area's etc). This makes them very hard to sneak up on, given them effective 360 degree perception. Information from Reading the Logs should be given as part of a normal Wits + Composure Roll, the range of this information is quiet short, only about 50 yards. This range can be extended by using the ability with focus. By spending a point of willpower, the creature can Read the Logs, anywhere within the distance they could travel in a day. In particular this can be used for tracking, without having to move. Given some form of idea of the Information Signiture of the target, (some existing point of reference they have left in the logs, locally) such a photograph, their legal name, or a place they have been (Penelties may apply if the Infomation Signiture is week, eg only a physical description) or the crypti having met them before, it may attempt a tracking roll with with Wits + Survival, this is a extended action. Since the cryptid doens't have to move in order to do the tracking it is much faster tan normal, taking only 5 minutes per roll. Angels are harder to spot, as the God Machine edits the logs to hide there presence. Even Angels not specifically designed to be concealed have a -2 on Perception Rolls to spot angels, and the +2 target successes on Extended Actions to track them. Demons are even harder, see Spoofing.</pre> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}